-- the definitions compiled code keeps as calls (sched-holds): every one reached from the entry, other
-- than the entry, that is a function on first-order data and is not a leaf (a body of at most 24
-- nodes as written is copied into its caller). A kept definition is compiled once, as its own function,
-- and its arguments are computed once by the caller: normalizing it into its caller instead substitutes
-- each argument at every use of the parameter, so a parameter used k times computes its argument k
-- times and the code grows by the argument's size k times over, at every level of the call tree
hold-ok : Word → Word → Bool
hold-ok e g =
  if %weq e g then false
  else (case def-type-code g return (λ _ → Bool) of
          none → false
          some T → (if fo-fun T
                      then (case def-source g return (λ _ → Bool) of
                              none → false
                              some c → %wlt #24 (c-weight c-fuel c #0))
                      else false))
